Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-11
Subject: Guard macro scanner rewind when no input buffer is active
License: expat

`compiler/symcreat.pas` builds synthetic method bodies by replacing the
current scanner with a fresh macro scanner and then calling
`tscannerfile.substitutemacro`. That fresh scanner has no active input
buffer yet: `tscannerfile.create` initializes `inputpointer` to nil, and
`replace_scanner` does not call `firstfile` before installing the macro text.

`substitutemacro` rewinds `inputpointer` before swapping in the macro file so
ordinary callers preserve the current character position. For a fresh macro
scanner there is no current character to rewind. Guard the rewind the same
way `startreplaytokens` already does, so synthetic-method parsing can install
its macro text without first decrementing a nil pointer.

1. replace_scanner creates a new tscannerfile.
2. inputpointer := nil
3. inputbuffer := nil
4. symcreat immediately calls substitutemacro(...) on that scanner.
5. First line in substitutemacro: dec(inputpointer);

C++20 rule is [expr.add] 7.6.6 paragraph 4:
For pointer P and integral J, C++20 defines only these cases:

1. P is null and J == 0: result is null.
2. Otherwise P points into an array object and the result stays within [0, n].
3. Otherwise behavior is undefined.

--- a/compiler/scanner.pas
+++ b/compiler/scanner.pas
@@ -3559,7 +3555,8 @@
         hp : tinputfile;
       begin
         { save old postion }
-        dec(inputpointer);
+        if assigned(inputpointer) then
+          dec(inputpointer);
         tempcloseinputfile;
       { create macro 'file' }
         { use special name to dispose after !! }
